@startuml
' WHAT ACTUALLY HAPPENS TO ONE SEED — the inside of a single pivot_extract call.
' Read left to right as time. Everything before "Extract" exists so that a hostile, dead or
' Cloudflare-fronted target still produces a verdict instead of silence.
!include _theme.puml

participant "**Recall**\n<size:10>have we seen it?</size>" as R
participant "**Gate**\n<size:10>audit.gate</size>" as G
participant "**Acquire**\n<size:10>escalate, then fall back</size>" as A
participant "**Extract**\n<size:10>the Pivot Matrix</size>" as E
participant "**Enrich**\n<size:10>keyed reverse lookups</size>" as N
participant "**Persist**\n<size:10>cases/<case>/</size>" as P

R -> R : search cases/*/raw/ across **every** case
note right of R
  A seed already collected returns CACHED —
  the cheapest possible answer, and it tells you
  the host is already in another case.
end note

R -> G : proceed?
G -> G : hostile target, no passive mode, no proxy?
note right of G #FBF0EF
  **Refused.** Fetching a hostile host from your own IP
  tells the operator they are under investigation.
end note

G -> A : allowed
A -> A : direct GET
A -> A : rotate-ua  ->  proxy  ->  render  ->  FlareSolverr
A -> A : still cold? Wayback snapshot, then urlscan stored DOM
note right of A
  A cold seed never ends on silence: if every path fails,
  fallback_probe returns PIVOTABLE (with surviving leads)
  or NO-PIVOT-YET (with next steps).
end note

A -> E : DOM (live, rendered or archived)
E -> E : favicon · trackers · wallets · Telegram · QR
E -> E : TLS cert + **JARM** · CORS backends · mail/SPF/DMARC
E -> E : keyless RDAP WHOIS · Wayback CDX timeline
E -> E : own JS/CSS bundles, source maps, SPA routes
E -> E : hosted PDFs/images -> /Info, XMP, EXIF
E -> E : **URL path -> kit directory + template**
E -> E : **raw capture** — DOM + every JS/CSS, hashed

E -> N : artifacts
N -> N : FOFA · urlscan · Censys · Shodan · WhoisXML reverse
N -> N : **IntelX** — stealer-log pass FIRST, then general
note right of N #FDF8EC
  Every absent key is DECLARED. A keyless run
  says what it could not query, so "nothing found"
  is never mistaken for "nothing exists".
end note

N -> P : one JSON per host
P -> P : raw/<host>.json · evidence/captures/ · tool_calls.jsonl
@enduml
